name: vigo-docker-keepalive-retract
description: >-
  Retraction module for vigo-docker-keepalive. Disabling Docker on a
  vigosrv host stops the control-plane, so this retract leaves docker
  enabled by default. Operators who want to genuinely shut Docker down
  should `systemctl disable --now docker` by hand after first stopping
  the vigosrv container.

resources: []

# Install resources that needed no retraction:
#   service: ensure-docker-running        — leave enabled; vigosrv depends on it
#   exec:    verify-compose-file-present  — pure check; nothing to undo
